// Shared material presets (style.md section 3.2), loaded by rv::assets::MaterialLibrary.
// Colors are sRGB hex art-direction starting points (style.md section 3), converted to linear on load.
// Physical plausibility: dielectrics use metallic 0 and roughness 0.3-0.95; metals use metallic 0.9-1.0 and their
// base color is the specular tint. Unlit materials are rendered as base color (times texture) scaled by
// emissiveStrength (see rv/assets/material_library.hpp).
// Procedural textures ("procedural:<surface>/<map>", rv/assets/surface_textures.hpp, generated at startup): the "full"
// surfaces carry the material's albedo and roughness themselves, tuned around its style section 3 color (named in each
// entry's comment), so their materials use a white base color and roughness and metallic factors of 1 (0 for
// dielectrics' metallic); the aged plastic "detail" surface modulates the plastics' own colors and roughness around 1.
// Furniture and room uvs are in meters (wood: 1 m per repeat along the board; floor and walls: room_shell
// metersPerTile 2, the 2 m repeat of the floor planks and the plaster).
